janet throgmerton has been an educator  at fancy farm elementary school for 25  years  and a principal for 11 years  now the principal known as miss janet  that's no nonsense made headlines after  she took on  a new role as a bus driver and she  started driving the bus in order to help  students get home  after school during the pandemic so  without further ado i would love to  welcome miss janet to the show  hello hi principal  janet hello i'm so excited you can call  me miss janet that's what all the kids  call me now  miss janet i read a quote of yours  saying  that um schools must care for  the whole child what do you mean by that  may i ask  well you know we we're here to teach  kids  there's lots of academic skills that we  want them to have  but before they can learn anything  we have to make sure that their needs  are met not only here at school but  if they have needs at home and  especially you know during the pandemic  we need to be sure that all the things  that they need  are met so that they don't have any  obstacles to have to overcome  and can concentrate on the learning and  so that's what we mean by the whole  child but then you even went further and  started driving  the bus to pick kids up who weren't  getting to school can you tell me about  that  yes so um three years ago i got my cdl  to help drive field trips so it wouldn't  cost our schools so much  and so in doing that i made a deal with  the transportation director that  they would train me for my cdl and i  would also  substitute drive in the afternoons as  needed because drivers were already  in a shortage even before the pandemic  and then  once um once coveted hit i had two  drivers that  contracted covid uh one of them has uh  won her battle against copen and i have  another that's still in the hospital  um on on event and so after that  um i stepped in to drive every afternoon  uh for our kids to get home and and  today i started driving in the morning  as well so  it's definitely um added to my job  but i enjoy it because it ensures that  our kids  get to and from school safely and we  have them here  so they can learn now miss janet  i i think i'm having one of those days  where  i just i feel like i'm back in march  it's been  really difficult we've had a lot of  setbacks  it's been really scary i think you know  we kind of around the holidays people  traveled  i think there's the new strain what do  you say i want to be one of your  students right now  and tell me what you say to students and  parents to  calm them or to encourage them to be  strong and just put one foot in front of  the other right now  well we we've been offering  opportunities uh by appointment for  parents to come into our building  and to see how we have set kids six feet  apart and we're wearing masks and we're  doing those things  and then when school is in session we  are doing everything that we can  to sanitize uh to be um  as sanitary as we can in the cafeteria  in our restrooms  but we know that it's scary  but we also know that our lives have to  find a way to move on  yeah and so i try to assure them that um  you know we love their kids as much as  they love their kids and want to  do what's best for them so yeah you know  definitely those things  well i think that the way that you care  for the whole child  is really um a model that i can  appreciate as a parent  uh sometimes you know i hear kids aren't  meeting expectations i've heard it about  my own kids  it's like the last thing you want to  hear right now you're like  are you kidding and it's just it's all  so difficult  so to know that these children are with  someone  who is cognizant about you know  things other than just learning but  their emotional state the safety  standards the getting  to and from school if you care about the  whole child  i think you are conquering the whole  picture  and we have some friends at this company  called erin condren and they heard about  what you were doing  and just wanted to step in and say thank  you  and they're a lifestyle brand and  they're known for organizational  essentials  in the home and the office i happen to  be very passionate about organization  it's one thing i can control as i grow  up and become  better organized and they want to donate  fifteen thousand dollars  worth of supplies uh to the faculty  and the students um including pens  notebooks walls calendars which is a  personal favorite of mine coloring books  and face masks  to you and your school thank you so much  that is so awesome  kids love gifts we we love to give  thanks to kids and teachers love gifts  too so they'll be super excited  we appreciate that so much and it's  supplies everybody can use and  really all of us at you know this show  and erin condren  were all just amazed by your story and  i can tell you as a human and a parent  thank you for everything that you're  doing thank you  miss janet thank you  [Music]
 

